2118 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 2119 0 R/Alt(Two inhibitory-jitter manipulations at the same jitter magnitude, sigma 14 ms, that both hold the mean inhibitory rate fixed. Left column (per-cell jitter): rasters show bursts smeared into a continuous shunt, and the excitatory rate falls to near zero while accuracy falls to chance. Right column (cycle-coherent jitter): whole bursts are displaced but within-burst synchrony is preserved, the excitatory rate rises from about 17 to about 73 Hz, and accuracy holds high. The bottom sweep panels overlay the realised mean inhibitory rate as a grey line, flat where the two arms are compared. Identical mean inhibition, opposite excitatory outcome.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 14300 0 R>>
endobj
